  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Component Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently defining the component architecture for Digital Saathi, focusing on modularity. I\'m starting with `src/types.ts` to define the necessary page IDs like \'home\' and \'basics\'. This foundational step will guide the creation of individual components and ensure clear organization.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve expanded the data structures in the codebase. I\'ve defined new data structures for translations, scam scenarios, and quiz questions. Specifically, I\'ve created interfaces for scam scenarios and quiz questions, and a translations interface to handle multi-language support. I am also working on interactive scam examples with a local context, which I think will make them more engaging and effective. I am now working on 10 beginner-friendly questions that test different areas.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Search**\n\nI\'m now integrating instant search functionality. I\'m focusing on `src/data/searchTopics.ts` to create an index for quick topic lookups. The search will allow users to jump directly to lessons or view explainer popups for terms like \"UPI PIN\" and \"DigiLocker\". I\'m also planning clear explanations after answers, score summaries, and customized encouragement for the quiz.\n\n\n**Constructing User Interface**\n\nI\'m now building out the user interface, starting with comprehensive documentation for the open-source CEP project. I\'ve drafted a detailed README covering the problem statement, target audience, and architecture. I\'ve also incorporated instructions on how to run the project, and an MIT license. I\'m focusing on key views: the home view has a welcoming hero, informative cards, and a new \"Can You Spot the Scam?\" simulator. The digital basics view covers smartphone and internet fundamentals.\n\n\n**Designing Safety Content**\n\nI\'m deep in designing safety content. I\'m focusing on digital payments, and I\'ve started building out a visual guide to UPI, breaking down the process into 7 simple steps with an interactive mockup. I\'m also highlighting critical \"Golden Safety Rules\" with high-contrast visual alerts, and an interactive simulation on how scammers trick people by misusing the UPI PIN. I\'m also planning to cover QR code safety, and dive into online safety with sections on phishing, SMS spoofing, OTP scams, and fake links. Additionally, I\'m thinking of interactive visual smartphone anatomy and a permission checker.\n\n\n**Crafting Safety Resources**\n\nI\'m now crafting safety resources. I\'m focusing on interactive content, like \"Do\'s & Don\'ts\" cards comparing safe and unsafe practices. I\'m building out scenarios for common scams, including fake customer care scams, and fake job/task scams that use social engineering. I\'m also preparing an emergency action plan for suspected scams, with actions to take immediately. I am also working on interactive quiz.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 348628992
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
