    user_response: "REDESIGN THE FRONTEND OF THE EXISTING DIGITAL SAATHI WEBSITE.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nKeep the current features, pages, content structure, and functionality. Do NOT turn this into a completely different product.\n\nThe main problem with the current design is the VISUAL STYLE.\n\nThe current frontend looks too much like a generic AI-generated SaaS/AI startup website:\n- Too many rounded cards\n- Too many gradients\n- Too much purple/blue\n- Generic floating UI elements\n- Generic AI illustrations\n- Excessive glassmorphism\n- Overly soft shadows\n- \"AI landing page\" appearance\n- Too many visual elements competing for attention\n\nREMOVE THAT ENTIRE VISUAL LANGUAGE.\n\nThe goal is to create a website that feels:\nMODERN + MINIMAL + TRENDY + CLASSIC + HUMAN + PREMIUM\n\nThink:\nmodern editorial website + polished technology product + contemporary digital education platform.\n\nNOT:\nAI startup landing page\nSaaS dashboard\nfintech startup\ngeneric template\nmodern caf\303\251 brand\ngaming website\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCORE DESIGN DIRECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nMake the website feel intentionally designed by a professional product designer.\n\nPrioritize:\n- Typography\n- Spacing\n- Layout\n- Visual hierarchy\n- Composition\n- Subtle interactions\n- Strong use of whitespace\n- High-quality imagery\n- Consistent visual language\n\nDo NOT try to make the website impressive by adding more components.\n\nInstead, make it impressive through restraint.\n\nUse fewer elements, but make every element feel intentional.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCOLOR SYSTEM\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nMove away from the current bright purple/blue AI aesthetic.\n\nUse a sophisticated neutral base:\n\n- Off-white / warm white background\n- Charcoal / near-black text\n- Very subtle gray borders\n- One restrained accent color\n\nPossible accent direction:\n- muted electric blue\nOR\n- muted indigo\nOR\n- deep green\n\nChoose ONE accent and use it consistently.\n\nAvoid:\n- Purple-to-blue gradients\n- Neon colors\n- Rainbow gradients\n- Excessive colored cards\n- Bright glowing effects\n\nThe website should mostly feel monochromatic with controlled accent usage.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTYPOGRAPHY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nTypography should become one of the main visual elements.\n\nUse a strong modern sans-serif typeface such as:\n- Inter\n- Geist\n- Manrope\n- Satoshi\n- Plus Jakarta Sans\n\nUse:\n- Large confident headlines\n- Medium-weight subheadings\n- Highly readable body text\n- Tight but intentional heading line-height\n\nDo NOT use huge \"AI startup\" typography that takes up half the screen.\n\nThe typography should feel editorial and sophisticated.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nNAVBAR\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nRedesign the navbar to be extremely clean.\n\nStructure:\n\nDigital Saathi logo/name\nHome\nBasics\nPayments\nSafety\nServices\nQuiz\nAbout\n\nRight side:\nA-   A   A+\nStart Learning\n\nDo NOT put every item inside pills.\n\nAvoid excessive rounded buttons.\n\nUse:\n- simple text navigation\n- subtle hover states\n- thin underline or small accent indicator for active page\n- one primary CTA\n\nNavbar should feel lightweight and almost disappear into the page.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nHERO SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCompletely redesign the current hero.\n\nDo NOT use:\n- floating cards everywhere\n- random badges\n- fake user avatars\n- excessive gradients\n- generic 3D illustrations\n- AI-generated abstract blobs\n- floating UI screenshots\n\nInstead create a strong editorial hero.\n\nSuggested structure:\n\nSmall eyebrow:\nDIGITAL SAATHI\n\nMain heading:\n\nMaking technology\neasier for everyone.\n\nShort description:\n\nSimple guides to help people understand everyday digital services, make safer online payments, identify scams, and navigate the digital world with confidence.\n\nPrimary CTA:\nStart Learning \342\206\222\n\nSecondary CTA:\nExplore Safety\n\nOn the right side, use ONE strong visual.\n\nPrefer:\n- a high-quality real-world photograph\n- a clean smartphone/product visual\n- or a carefully composed editorial illustration\n\nThe visual should communicate:\ntechnology + accessibility + real people.\n\nIt should NOT look like a generic AI-generated SaaS hero image.\n\nThe hero should have lots of whitespace.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nHERO COMPOSITION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDo NOT force everything into cards.\n\nUse a strong asymmetric layout.\n\nExample:\n\nLEFT:\nsmall label\nlarge headline\ndescription\nbuttons\n\nRIGHT:\nsingle strong visual\n\nThe visual can slightly overlap the hero boundary, but keep it subtle.\n\nThe overall composition should feel closer to a modern editorial/product website than a SaaS landing page.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nFEATURE SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nKeep the existing four categories:\n\nDigital Basics\nDigital Payments\nOnline Safety\nDigital Services\n\nBut redesign them.\n\nDO NOT make four colorful floating cards.\n\nInstead create a more sophisticated grid/list.\n\nExample:\n\n01  Digital Basics\n    Learn smartphone, internet and app basics.\n    Explore \342\206\222\n\n02  Digital Payments\n    Understand UPI, QR payments and safe transactions.\n    Explore \342\206\222\n\n03  Online Safety\n    Identify scams, phishing and suspicious messages.\n    Explore \342\206\222\n\n04  Digital Services\n    Learn about important online services and documents.\n    Explore \342\206\222\n\nUse:\n- thin borders\n- subtle dividers\n- generous spacing\n- typography\n- small icons only where useful\n\nThe section should feel editorial and structured.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINTERACTIVE SCAM SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nKEEP the scam detector feature.\n\nBut redesign it so it feels like part of the product instead of a random floating widget.\n\nCreate a dedicated section titled:\n\nCan you spot the scam?\n\nShow a realistic simulated message/email/SMS in a clean interface.\n\nExample:\n\n\"URGENT!\nYour bank account will be blocked today.\nClick this link to complete your KYC.\"\n\nThen:\n\nIs this safe?\n\n[ Scam ]    [ Safe ]\n\nAfter selecting an answer, reveal:\n\nWhy?\n\n- Creates unnecessary urgency\n- Uses suspicious language\n- Contains an unknown link\n- Requests immediate action\n\nMake the interaction smooth and minimal.\n\nDo NOT make it look like a game.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDIGITAL BASICS / PAYMENTS / SAFETY / SERVICES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nKeep the existing educational content.\n\nHowever, redesign the internal pages to follow the same visual system.\n\nUse:\n- large headings\n- short explanations\n- numbered steps\n- diagrams\n- screenshots where useful\n- simple icons\n- clear spacing\n\nAvoid putting every piece of content inside a card.\n\nUse cards only when they actually improve hierarchy.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUIZ PAGE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nKeep the existing quiz functionality.\n\nRedesign it to look like a clean learning experience.\n\nUse:\n\nQuestion 01 / 10\n\nQuestion text\n\nAnswer options\n\nProgress indicator\n\nNext \342\206\222\n\nAt the end:\n\nYour score\n8 / 10\n\nand a simple recommendation.\n\nAvoid colorful gamification.\n\nKeep it sophisticated and educational.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nABOUT PAGE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nKeep the existing project information.\n\nMake it feel like an editorial project page.\n\nInclude:\n\nDigital Saathi\n\nWhy we built this\nThe problem\nOur approach\nOpen-source vision\n\nUse large typography, short paragraphs, statistics only when verified, and simple visual storytelling.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMICRO INTERACTIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAdd subtle modern interactions:\n\n- smooth hover transitions\n- slight image movement\n- text underline animations\n- button arrow movement\n- section reveal on scroll\n- subtle navigation transitions\n\nBut keep animations restrained.\n\nNO:\n- excessive floating animations\n- bouncing elements\n- glowing effects\n- parallax everywhere\n- animated gradients\n- excessive motion\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBORDERS / CARDS / SHAPES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUse fewer rounded containers.\n\nCurrent design relies too heavily on rounded cards.\n\nInstead use:\n- straight/soft rectangular sections\n- thin 1px borders\n- subtle dividers\n- occasional 8\342\200\22312px radius\n- large open layouts\n\nAvoid:\n- giant pill buttons everywhere\n- excessive 20\342\200\22330px rounded cards\n- glassmorphism\n- frosted glass\n- floating panels\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nIMAGERY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf images are used, prioritize authentic photography or carefully selected editorial visuals.\n\nImages should represent:\n- real people using smartphones\n- digital learning\n- elderly/first-time technology users\n- everyday digital services\n- online safety\n\nAvoid generic:\n- AI robot illustrations\n- abstract 3D shapes\n- floating holograms\n- futuristic technology graphics\n- generic startup illustrations\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRESPONSIVENESS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe design must remain excellent on:\n\nDesktop\nTablet\nMobile\n\nOn mobile:\n- simplify navigation\n- maintain typography hierarchy\n- stack sections naturally\n- keep buttons easy to tap\n- maintain generous spacing\n- never make the page feel cramped\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nACCESSIBILITY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nKeep the existing accessibility features:\n\nA-\nA\nA+\n\nMake them visually subtle.\n\nMaintain:\n- readable typography\n- strong contrast\n- keyboard accessibility\n- visible focus states\n- meaningful alt text\n- simple language\n- accessible buttons\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMOST IMPORTANT DESIGN RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDO NOT ADD MORE FEATURES.\n\nThe current features are already sufficient.\n\nSpend the effort on making the FRONTEND LOOK BETTER.\n\nThe website should look like a carefully designed modern digital product, not something generated from an AI website template.\n\nThink:\n\n\"Someone spent time designing the typography, spacing and composition.\"\n\nNot:\n\n\"AI generated a landing page with cards and gradients.\"\n\nThe final aesthetic should be:\n\nMINIMAL\nEDITORIAL\nMODERN\nTIMELESS\nTECHNOLOGY-FOCUSED\nHUMAN\nACCESSIBLE\nCONFIDENT\n\nAvoid making it:\n- overly corporate\n- overly playful\n- overly futuristic\n- overly luxurious\n- caf\303\251/lifestyle-brand-like\n- generic AI/SaaS\n\nThe final website should feel like a serious, well-designed **digital public service / educational product**."
