  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///README.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    replacement_chunks {
      replacement_content: "# Digital Saathi \342\200\224 Making Technology Easier for Everyone\n\n> **An Open-Source Digital Literacy & Cyber Safety Awareness Initiative**  \n> Developed for a 3rd-Year BSc Computer Science Community Engagement Project (CEP)  \n> Theme: *\342\200\234Building Open-Source Solutions for Social Problems\342\200\235*\n\n---\n\n## 1. Problem Statement\n\nAs digital services, UPI banking, and mobile governance platforms become essential in India, millions of senior citizens, first-time smartphone users, and non-technical demographics struggle with digital navigation. This knowledge gap leads to:\n- High vulnerability to phishing scams, fake KYC warnings, and payment fraud.\n- Loss of daily autonomy and constant dependence on others.\n- Anxiety and fear of making critical mistakes when using technology.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Project Objectives\n\n- **Demystify Technology:** Provide plain-language, jargon-free explanations for smartphones, browsers, and mobile apps.\n- **Empower Safe Payments:** Clarify how UPI works, highlighting that **receiving money NEVER requires entering a UPI PIN**.\n- **Scam Immunization:** Build intuitive scam recognition skills through interactive simulated exercises.\n- **Promote Civic Inclusion:** Educate citizens on official public tools like DigiLocker and Masked Aadhaar.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Modules & Features\n\n1. **Digital Basics:** Smartphone hardware controls, Wi-Fi vs mobile data, and app permission audits.\n2. **Digital Payments & UPI:** Visual 7-step payment process, QR code precautions, and the 4 Golden Rules of UPI.\n3. **Online Safety & Threat Defense:** Analysis of phishing, OTP scams, fake helplines, part-time task frauds, and comprehensive DOs/DON\'Ts.\n4. **Interactive Scam Spotter:** Hands-on simulated message analyzer with instant rationale and safety guidance.\n5. **Digital Public Services:** Safe usage of DigiLocker, identifying verified `.gov.in` portals, and Masked Aadhaar practices.\n6. **10-Question Knowledge Quiz:** Interactive self-assessment with score evaluation and topic-specific advice.\n7. **Accessibility Features:** Dynamic text sizing (`A`, `A+`, `A++`), high-contrast typography, and multilingual English/Hindi/Marathi previews.\n8. **Client-Side Quick Search:** Fast indexing for terms like UPI, OTP, DigiLocker, KYC, and Cyber Crime Helpline 1930.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n- **Frontend:** React 19 + TypeScript\n- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS (Modern minimal editorial design)\n- **Typography:** Instrument Sans, Plus Jakarta Sans & Noto Sans Devanagari\n- **Icons:** Lucide Icons\n- **Build System:** Vite\n\n---\n\n## 5. Local Setup & Execution\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone https://github.com/digital-saathi/digital-saathi.git\n\n# Navigate to project directory\ncd digital-saathi\n\n# Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# Start the local development server\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Emergency Support\n\n- **National Cyber Crime Helpline (India):** Dial `1930`\n- **National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal:** [https://cybercrime.gov.in](https://cybercrime.gov.in)\n\n---\n\n## 7. License\n\nThis project is licensed under the **MIT License** \342\200\224 feel free to fork, adapt, translate, and deploy for non-commercial community awareness.\n"
    }
