  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the frontend redesign of **Digital Saathi**, crafting a modern, minimal, and human-centered editorial design system tailored for digital literacy and cyber safety:\n\n- **Editorial Visual Identity**: Replaced generic gradients, floating cards, and glassmorphism with a warm neutral canvas (`#FAF9F6`), high-contrast charcoal typography, thin 1px borders, and generous whitespace.\n- **Clean Asymmetrical Hero**: Implemented a confident headline paired with an annotated Digital Safety Compass visual, highlighting foundational principles (UPI PIN security, OTP confidentiality, and `.gov.in` verification).\n- **Refined Navigation & Accessibility**: Built a lightweight navbar featuring text navigation, active indicator lines, accessible text scaling controls (`A` | `A+` | `A++`), client-side topic search (`\342\214\230K`), and multi-language support (English, Hindi, Marathi).\n- **Structured Learning Modules**: Redesigned all educational curricula into numbered, scannable guides with diagrams and checklists:\n  - `01 Digital Basics`: Smartphone controls, Wi-Fi vs. mobile data, and app permission audits.\n  - `02 Digital Payments & UPI`: Visual 7-step payment process and the 4 Golden Rules of UPI.\n  - `03 Online Safety`: Scam breakdowns (Phishing, OTP fraud, Fake customer care, Task scams) with a comprehensive DOs & DON\'Ts matrix.\n  - `04 Digital Public Services`: DigiLocker document storage, Masked Aadhaar practices, and official `.gov.in` domain verification.\n- **Interactive Scam Spotter & Knowledge Assessment**: Integrated a realistic message verification simulator and a 10-question quiz with instant rationales and personalized recommendations.\n- **Academic & Open-Source Focus**: Formatted the About page and project documentation around the 3rd-Year BSc Computer Science Community Engagement Project (CEP) mission, including National Cyber Crime Helpline `1930` emergency protocols and an MIT open-source repository overview."
    modified_response: "I have completed the frontend redesign of **Digital Saathi**, crafting a modern, minimal, and human-centered editorial design system tailored for digital literacy and cyber safety:\n\n- **Editorial Visual Identity**: Replaced generic gradients, floating cards, and glassmorphism with a warm neutral canvas (`#FAF9F6`), high-contrast charcoal typography, thin 1px borders, and generous whitespace.\n- **Clean Asymmetrical Hero**: Implemented a confident headline paired with an annotated Digital Safety Compass visual, highlighting foundational principles (UPI PIN security, OTP confidentiality, and `.gov.in` verification).\n- **Refined Navigation & Accessibility**: Built a lightweight navbar featuring text navigation, active indicator lines, accessible text scaling controls (`A` | `A+` | `A++`), client-side topic search (`\342\214\230K`), and multi-language support (English, Hindi, Marathi).\n- **Structured Learning Modules**: Redesigned all educational curricula into numbered, scannable guides with diagrams and checklists:\n  - `01 Digital Basics`: Smartphone controls, Wi-Fi vs. mobile data, and app permission audits.\n  - `02 Digital Payments & UPI`: Visual 7-step payment process and the 4 Golden Rules of UPI.\n  - `03 Online Safety`: Scam breakdowns (Phishing, OTP fraud, Fake customer care, Task scams) with a comprehensive DOs & DON\'Ts matrix.\n  - `04 Digital Public Services`: DigiLocker document storage, Masked Aadhaar practices, and official `.gov.in` domain verification.\n- **Interactive Scam Spotter & Knowledge Assessment**: Integrated a realistic message verification simulator and a 10-question quiz with instant rationales and personalized recommendations.\n- **Academic & Open-Source Focus**: Formatted the About page and project documentation around the 3rd-Year BSc Computer Science Community Engagement Project (CEP) mission, including National Cyber Crime Helpline `1930` emergency protocols and an MIT open-source repository overview."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
