  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Component Structures**\n\nOkay, I\'m deep diving into the component structures. I\'m examining files like `HomePage.tsx`, `BasicsPage.tsx`, and `Footer.tsx` to understand the architecture and how these pieces fit together. I\'m also looking into `ScamSpotter.tsx`, `SearchModal.tsx`, and associated data files to gauge data flow and component interactions. I\'m focusing on how content is organized and presented.\n\n\n**Identifying Localization Issues**\n\nI\'ve discovered a significant localization issue. I found that many components like `HomePage.tsx` and others, contain hardcoded English content. Despite language selection, most body text, cards, guides, and the ScamSpotter remain in English even when Hindi or Marathi are selected. The user\'s request for complete translation across all pages is not met. I am focusing on cataloging the untranslated elements for each page and component. This includes hero content, learning modules, and scam detection sections.\n\n\n**Cataloging Missing Translations**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the missing translations within specific pages. I see untranslated elements in `BasicsPage.tsx` including headers and smartphone guides. The `PaymentsPage.tsx` also has untranslated content in the UPI guides. The `SafetyPage.tsx` contains untranslated descriptions of cyber threats and safety rules. Finally, `ServicesPage.tsx` includes untranslated descriptions of public services.\n\n\n"
