  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Icon Options**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started exploring Lucide icons for potential import, specifically considering `KeyRound`, `ShieldAlert`, `AlertTriangle`, and others. My focus is on suitability and coverage. Now, I\'m getting ready to update `BasicsPage.tsx` with these new findings.\n\n\n**Designing Content Structure**\n\nI\'m now deep in content design, working on `basicsContent.en`, `.hi`, and `.mr`. The focus is enriching the `s3` section with a detailed breakdown of PIN vulnerabilities, including dangerous patterns and the risks associated with weak PINs. I\'m also adding a comprehensive `simSecurity` section, to highlight crucial security measures for SIM cards.\n\n\n**Crafting Explanations Now**\n\nI\'m currently crafting detailed explanations for the SIM security section. I\'m focusing on the \"why\" and \"how\" of SIM lock, and breaking down the Android and iOS steps in clear, concise language. I\'ve structured content around `whyTitle`, `whyDesc`, `howTitle`, and `howDesc` as the cornerstone of the explanation. I\'m also adding `stepsAndroidTitle`, `stepsAndroid`, `stepsIosTitle`, and `stepsIos` for platform-specific guidance.\n\n\n**Verifying Language Clarity**\n\nI\'m now revising the PUK warning content, specifically the title and description, including updates to the `dos` and `donts` sections. I am making sure the language is very clear and concise, with an eye towards accurate Hindi translation. I am also working on creating a new section in Hindi and verifying existing translations. My focus is on ensuring linguistic accuracy and cultural appropriateness in both the Hindi and Marathi translations.\n\n\n**Analyzing PIN Vulnerabilities**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the content related to weak PIN vulnerabilities. I\'m translating key concepts like \"Risks of weak PINs\" and \"Examples of dangerous PINs\" into Hindi. This includes translating the explanation, \"If your phone or wallet is stolen, the thief can try to unlock the phone by looking at your date of birth from your Aadhaar card or driving license and entering 1234, 0000, or the year of birth. As soon as the phone opens, your bank and UPI apps are at risk.\" I am also translating examples of weak PINs such as sequential digits, repeated digits, birth year, direct keypad line, car number or last 4 digits of mobile number.\n\n\n**Refining Security Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating content about robust SIM security measures. I\'ve focused on \"6-digit random PIN or alphanumeric password + fingerprint lock\" as a robust approach, including the SIM lock and physical ejection aspects. I\'m focusing on crafting the crucial SIM security aspects, including the implications of simple phone screen locks, and the ease with which a SIM can be removed and misused. I\'ve detailed the risks, solution of using SIM lock features with Android and iOS steps in Hindi.\n\n\n**Translating Instructions Now**\n\nI\'m translating the iOS SIM PIN steps into Hindi, focusing on clarity: \"\340\244\270\340\245\207\340\244\237\340\244\277\340\244\202\340\244\227\340\245\215\340\244\270 \342\236\224 \340\244\256\340\245\213\340\244\254\340\244\276\340\244\207\340\244\262 \340\244\241\340\245\207\340\244\237\340\244\276 (Cellular) \342\236\224 SIM PIN \342\236\224 SIM PIN \340\244\232\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\245\202 \340\244\225\340\244\260\340\245\207\340\244\202 \342\236\224 \340\244\205\340\244\252\340\244\250\340\244\276 4-\340\244\205\340\244\202\340\244\225\340\245\213\340\244\202 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\252\340\244\277\340\244\250 \340\244\270\340\245\207\340\244\237 \340\244\225\340\244\260\340\245\207\340\244\202\340\245\244\" I\'m also ensuring the default PIN and PUK code warnings are clear. I\'m focusing on the Marathi translation: \"\340\244\256\340\245\213\340\244\254\340\244\276\340\244\210\340\244\262 \340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\202\340\244\265\340\244\276 \340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\225\340\245\200\340\244\237 \340\244\227\340\244\271\340\244\276\340\244\263 \340\244\235\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\270 \340\244\232\340\245\213\340\244\260 \340\244\206\340\244\247\340\244\276\340\244\260 \340\244\225\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\215\340\244\241 \340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\202\340\244\265\340\244\276 \340\244\241\340\245\215\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\257\340\244\265\340\245\215\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\202\340\244\227 \340\244\262\340\244\276\340\244\257\340\244\270\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\270\340\244\265\340\244\260\340\245\200\340\244\262 \340\244\234\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\256\340\244\244\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200\340\244\226 \340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\271\340\245\202\340\244\250 \340\244\253\340\245\213\340\244\250 \340\244\205\340\244\250\340\244\262\340\245\211\340\244\225 \340\244\225\340\244\260\340\244\243\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\232\340\244\276 \340\244\252\340\245\215\340\244\260\340\244\257\340\244\244\340\245\215\340\244\250 \340\244\225\340\244\260\340\244\244\340\244\276\340\244\244. \340\244\253\340\245\213\340\244\250 \340\244\205\340\244\250\340\244\262\340\245\211\340\244\225 \340\244\235\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\270 Google Pay \340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\202\340\244\265\340\244\276 PhonePe \340\244\247\340\245\213\340\244\225\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\244 \340\244\257\340\245\207\340\244\212 \340\244\266\340\244\225\340\244\244\340\245\207.\"\n\n\n**Detailing Content Now**\n\nI\'m now detailing PIN vulnerabilities, adding examples in Marathi: sequential, repeated digits, birth year, keypad lines, and vehicle/mobile digits. I\'m emphasizing the benefits of a robust security: six-digit PIN or password and fingerprint lock. I\'ve also detailed SIM lock importance to help prevent theft scenarios, specifically noting that screen locks are not enough protection.\n\n\n"
