  planner_response {
    response: "The UI/UX of **Digital Saathi** has been redesigned with a focus on accessibility, clarity, and trust for older adults, parents, grandparents, and first-time smartphone users.\n\n### Key Design & Usability Updates\n\n- **Accessible Visual System & Typography**:\n  - Implemented a warm off-white canvas (`#FAF8F5`) paired with deep charcoal text (`#111827`) and a calming deep teal accent (`#0D5C58`).\n  - Integrated high-readability typography (`Inter`, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, and `Noto Sans Devanagari`) with generous line heights and high contrast (WCAG AA compliant).\n\n- **Root Text-Scaling Controls (A / A+ / A++)**:\n  - Added text-size toggle controls to the top accessibility bar, allowing users to increase typography across the entire interface (16px, 18px, and 20px base sizes).\n\n- **Welcoming Hero & Daily Compass**:\n  - Structured the welcoming headline with plain language: *\"Making technology easier & safer for everyone.\"*\n  - Replaced floating cards with a single **Digital Safety Compass** highlighting essential daily safety rules (UPI PIN only for sending money, OTP confidentiality, verifying `.gov.in` domains) and immediate access to the National Cyber Crime Helpline (**1930**).\n\n- **Intent-Driven Navigation Grid**:\n  - Placed a **\"What would you like help with?\"** intent chooser directly below the hero, offering 4 clear, single-tap entry points:\n    1. \360\237\223\261 **Learn to use my phone** (*Digital Basics*)\n    2. \360\237\222\263 **Understand digital payments** (*Safe UPI & QR scanning*)\n    3. \360\237\233\241\357\270\217 **Stay safe from scams** (*Fraud defense & fake message spotting*)\n    4. \360\237\223\204 **Use online services** (*DigiLocker & official citizen portals*)\n\n- **Educational \"Before You Click\" Scam Spotter**:\n  - Redesigned simulated message exercises with clear buttons (*\"This looks suspicious\"* / *\"This looks safe\"*), step-by-step red flag breakdowns, and actionable safety tips.\n\n- **Refined Navigation & Footer**:\n  - Enhanced touch targets (minimum 44\342\200\22348px) with prominent language switcher buttons (**English | \340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200 | \340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200**).\n  - Streamlined the footer to highlight the **1930 Cyber Fraud Helpline** and structured learning guides with no technical jargon."
    thinking: "**Verifying Code Success**\n\nI\'ve got good news! The TypeScript compilation using `--noEmit` and `compile_applet` both completed without a hitch \342\200\223 zero errors reported. I\'m now moving on to verifying that the requested changes are indeed implemented. Key areas I\'m checking are audience focus, making sure it\'s warm, accessible, and tailored to seniors, parents, grandparents, and first-time smartphone users. The text size toggle is next on the list.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The UI/UX of **Digital Saathi** has been redesigned with a focus on accessibility, clarity, and trust for older adults, parents, grandparents, and first-time smartphone users.\n\n### Key Design & Usability Updates\n\n- **Accessible Visual System & Typography**:\n  - Implemented a warm off-white canvas (`#FAF8F5`) paired with deep charcoal text (`#111827`) and a calming deep teal accent (`#0D5C58`).\n  - Integrated high-readability typography (`Inter`, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, and `Noto Sans Devanagari`) with generous line heights and high contrast (WCAG AA compliant).\n\n- **Root Text-Scaling Controls (A / A+ / A++)**:\n  - Added text-size toggle controls to the top accessibility bar, allowing users to increase typography across the entire interface (16px, 18px, and 20px base sizes).\n\n- **Welcoming Hero & Daily Compass**:\n  - Structured the welcoming headline with plain language: *\"Making technology easier & safer for everyone.\"*\n  - Replaced floating cards with a single **Digital Safety Compass** highlighting essential daily safety rules (UPI PIN only for sending money, OTP confidentiality, verifying `.gov.in` domains) and immediate access to the National Cyber Crime Helpline (**1930**).\n\n- **Intent-Driven Navigation Grid**:\n  - Placed a **\"What would you like help with?\"** intent chooser directly below the hero, offering 4 clear, single-tap entry points:\n    1. \360\237\223\261 **Learn to use my phone** (*Digital Basics*)\n    2. \360\237\222\263 **Understand digital payments** (*Safe UPI & QR scanning*)\n    3. \360\237\233\241\357\270\217 **Stay safe from scams** (*Fraud defense & fake message spotting*)\n    4. \360\237\223\204 **Use online services** (*DigiLocker & official citizen portals*)\n\n- **Educational \"Before You Click\" Scam Spotter**:\n  - Redesigned simulated message exercises with clear buttons (*\"This looks suspicious\"* / *\"This looks safe\"*), step-by-step red flag breakdowns, and actionable safety tips.\n\n- **Refined Navigation & Footer**:\n  - Enhanced touch targets (minimum 44\342\200\22348px) with prominent language switcher buttons (**English | \340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200 | \340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200**).\n  - Streamlined the footer to highlight the **1930 Cyber Fraud Helpline** and structured learning guides with no technical jargon."
